            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Aliquamdiū pugnātum est; tum hostēs fūgērunt. There was fighting for some time; then the enemy fled."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "aliquam + diū (taught): for a fair while, longer than paulisper. Caesar uses it of battles."
            }
